## POSITION TYPE
**Type A — Single-driver thesis.**

Amprius is a single-product-category company (silicon anode batteries) serving a single primary value proposition (performance density leadership for electrical mobility). While it addresses multiple end markets (aviation UAV, light EV, defense), these are all downstream applications of the same core technology and manufacturing capability. Impairment of the silicon anode performance advantage — whether through competitive catch-up by CATL/BYD or a manufacturing quality failure — would impair all revenue streams simultaneously. There is no independent second driver that could offset a failure of the core technology thesis. Fixed cap ~35%.

---

## POSITION SIZING RECOMMENDATION
**Recommended maximum position size: 12%**

This is a Type A company with a hard cap of 35%, but several factors warrant sizing well below the cap. The company is pre-profitability with a negative 21% gross margin, burning approximately $2-3M/month in cash (with $48.4M remaining), and is reliant on ATM equity issuance ($8.5M this quarter, $57.8M remaining on the facility) to fund operations — meaning ongoing dilution is structural, not episodic. The thesis is strengthening and the technology differentiation is credible, but the path to gross margin breakeven is not yet visible on a timeline (Cycle is gross margin positive but the blended company margin is still deeply negative). The ex-China manufacturing diversification, which is a key risk mitigation claim, remains unproven and vague. A 12% position reflects conviction in the thesis direction while respecting the pre-profitability risk, dilution overhang, and single-driver concentration.

---

## RECOMMENDATION
**Add to 12%**

The thesis is Strengthening with No stumble. Per the decision matrix, this is an unambiguous Add. The specific measurable condition that would change this recommendation next quarter: if Q2 revenue does not show sequential growth (given the strong backlog and stated momentum), or if the ex-China contract manufacturing announcement does not materialize as promised ("very soon"), either would trigger a reassessment of management credibility and the tariff mitigation argument's strength.

---

## FRESH MONEY TEST
**Fresh money allocation: 8%**

The gap between 8% (fresh money) and 12% (recommended maximum) reflects the pre-profitability risk and dilution structure that an existing holder has already priced in through prior entry. A fresh buyer today faces: (1) no certainty on when blended gross margins turn positive, (2) ongoing ATM dilution that is structural, (3) a Colorado facility cancellation that signals the company cannot yet self-fund its own manufacturing ambitions, and (4) a customer concentration risk (three customers >10% of revenue) that is not yet resolved. The thesis is real and the technology differentiation is credible, but a fresh buyer should size conservatively until at least one of the following is demonstrated: blended gross margin breakeven, ex-China manufacturing operational, or a second large ($10M+) volume purchase order from a new customer segment. The gap is conviction-based, not inertia — an existing holder at 12% is holding on thesis strength; a fresh buyer should enter at 8% and scale on confirmation.

